  "body": "There is a general desire to have the option to write some code in Rust, especially performance sensitive code. Currently Synapse can optionally use the https://github.com/erikjohnston/rust-jaeger-python-client library when connecting to Jaeger, however we expect future Rust components would *not* be optional (to avoid having to maintain the same code in two different languages).\r\n\r\nSome things that we need to figure out before we can start doing this:\r\n\r\n- [x] Ensure that our package build systems correctly work with Rust dependencies.\r\n- [x] Where we keep the Rust code, and how we hook it into Synapse (e.g. is it in the same repo, are the Rust modules done as a separate python library, etc)\r\n- [x] How to hook Rust logging into python logging (probably [pyo3-log](https://github.com/vorner/pyo3-log) will just work)\r\n- [ ] How to call async functions to/from Rust (will [pyo3-asyncio](https://github.com/awestlake87/pyo3-asyncio) just work? Does it need us to use the asyncio reactor?)\r\n- [ ] How do we handle log contexts? How do we record CPU usage in Rust?\r\n\r\nIdeally we'd start with a trivial module as a PoC before tackling anything larger.",
